# Cloudflare Pages reads this file verbatim. Two jobs.
#
# 1. CACHING. The font files have stable names — `npm run fonts` writes the
#    same five paths every time — so without an explicit rule Cloudflare's
#    default sends a repeat visitor back to revalidate 190 KB of woff2 that
#    has not changed. Astro's own _astro/* names carry a content hash, so they
#    can be held forever too. Page HTML is deliberately left alone: it must
#    revalidate, or a deploy takes a day to reach anyone.
#
#    Core Web Vitals is a ranking signal and fonts are on the critical path,
#    which makes this an SEO line as much as a performance one.
#
# 2. HEADERS a static marketing site should send anyway. None of them change
#    what the page does; they just close doors nothing here needs open.

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/badges/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/og-tr.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
